Piece artwork
-------------

Only the sets listed here may be bundled. The upstream chessground package
declares about forty piece sets as Flutter assets, and Flutter cannot leave out
a dependency's assets, so depending on it directly would ship all of them.
Most are CC BY-NC-SA, "free for personal use" or of unknown origin, none of
which is compatible with a GPL app on a store. That is why this app uses a
vendored trimmed copy (above), and why the built bundle is checked against this
table. tool/asset_allowlist.txt is the machine-readable form of the first
column.

  Set      | Author                      | Licence | Source                                                          | Added in
  ---------+-----------------------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------------------+---------
  cburnett | Colin M. L. Burnett         | GPLv2+  | github.com/lichess-org/lila/tree/master/public/piece/cburnett   | WP-04
           |                             |         | (originally en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Cburnett)                |
  merida   | Armando Hernandez Marroquin | GPLv2+  | github.com/lichess-org/lila/tree/master/public/piece/merida     | WP-04
  rhosgfx  | RhosGFX                     | CC0 1.0 | github.com/lichess-org/lila/tree/master/public/piece/rhosgfx    | WP-04
           |                             |         | (originally rhosgfx.itch.io)                                    |

The licences are those stated in lila's COPYING.md
(github.com/lichess-org/lila/blob/master/COPYING.md), read on 2026-09-19. The
files in this repository are the WebP renderings (1x to 4x) that
flutter-chessground makes from lila's SVGs, taken from the commit named above.
"GPLv2+" means version 2 or any later version, so these two sets are used here
under GPL-3.0. CC0 asks for nothing; the credit is given anyway.

Checked and compatible, but not bundled: chessnut (Apache-2.0), fantasy /
spatial / celtic (MIT), mpchess (GPLv3+). Adding one means a row here, a line
in tool/asset_allowlist.txt, a value in BoardPieceSet, and a re-run of
third_party/sync_chessground.py.


Board themes
------------

Board themes are colour schemes defined in code. No board images are bundled:
the image boards in lila are AGPLv3+, which this app does not take on.


